WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.115
A shopper whose browser runs on Chicago time opens the store to look up when they placed their latest order, which they placed at 9:08 in the morning.

2
00:00:10.115 --> 00:00:14.534
From the home page, they click Sign in, and the Login page opens.

3
00:00:14.534 --> 00:00:24.115
They type alice as the username, fill in their sign-in details, and click Login, which brings them back to the home page, now signed in to their account.

4
00:00:24.115 --> 00:00:28.662
Signed in, they open My orders to find the order they placed this morning.

5
00:00:28.662 --> 00:00:46.158
My orders lists order number 1 for $149.99, and its Date now reads 11/16/2026 09:08:50: the same morning hour as on the shopper's own clock, in the same format as before.

6
00:00:46.158 --> 00:00:52.667
Shoppers now see each order's Date in their own time zone, so it matches the moment they actually placed it.
